      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✓ Transport — src/transport/web/ → server.ts + routes/ + app/ (React SPA). Telegram bot dir NOT in tree (deleted per CLAUDE.md note).\n✓ Core — src/tools/ has exactly: collections, items, outfits, photos, share, weather (6 files). types/index.ts + constants/ (categories, colors, themes).\n✓ AI — src/ai/ has 17 files incl. client.ts, parse.ts, instrumented.ts, embed/embedImage/embedBackfill, suggestEvents/discoverEvents.\n✓ DB — src/db/ → client.ts, schema.ts, queries.ts, migrations/, reconcileMigrations.ts, safeImport.mjs.\n✓ Storage — src/storage/ → images.ts, integrityCheck.ts, embeddings.ts.\n\n✓ Cross-cutting dirs DO exist:\n  src/auth/ → emailGuard, password, googleOAuth\n  src/billing/ → wallet, packs, stripe, swallow, tokenTable, openrouterKeys, constants, errors\n  src/jobs/ → scheduler, registry, pushNotify, pushStore, store, runStore, seed, types/\n  src/constants/themes.ts (yes — lives in core constants, not its own dir)\n\n⚠ MISMATCHES vs my drawing:\n  • Embeddings: I put under src/ai/ but also noted src/storage/embeddings.ts — both real. The DB table layer lives in storage/ (vector store-ish). The embedders live in ai/. Both correct.\n  • Themes: I drew it as its own cross-cutting concern but in tree it's a single file (src/constants/themes.ts) inside the core constants dir — smaller than the others. Plus a mirrored copy at src/transport/web/app/src/constants/theme.ts for the Docker build.\n  • src/weather/ (fetch.ts, wmo.ts) — a small standalone layer I didn't draw separately; it sits alongside core, called by tools/weather.ts.\n  • src/backups/ (backup cron) and src/settings.ts — infrastructure present in tree, not on my sketch.\n  • src/lib/, src/scripts/, src/tunnel.ts, src/combined.ts — utility/infra, not product layers.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 12,
      "containerId": "box_check",
      "originalText": "✓ Transport — src/transport/web/ → server.ts + routes/ + app/ (React SPA). Telegram bot dir NOT in tree (deleted per CLAUDE.md note).\n✓ Core — src/tools/ has exactly: collections, items, outfits, photos, share, weather (6 files). types/index.ts + constants/ (categories, colors, themes).\n✓ AI — src/ai/ has 17 files incl. client.ts, parse.ts, instrumented.ts, embed/embedImage/embedBackfill, suggestEvents/discoverEvents.\n✓ DB — src/db/ → client.ts, schema.ts, queries.ts, migrations/, reconcileMigrations.ts, safeImport.mjs.\n✓ Storage — src/storage/ → images.ts, integrityCheck.ts, embeddings.ts.\n\n✓ Cross-cutting dirs DO exist:\n  src/auth/ → emailGuard, password, googleOAuth\n  src/billing/ → wallet, packs, stripe, swallow, tokenTable, openrouterKeys, constants, errors\n  src/jobs/ → scheduler, registry, pushNotify, pushStore, store, runStore, seed, types/\n  src/constants/themes.ts (yes — lives in core constants, not its own dir)\n\n⚠ MISMATCHES vs my drawing:\n  • Embeddings: I put under src/ai/ but also noted src/storage/embeddings.ts — both real. The DB table layer lives in storage/ (vector store-ish). The embedders live in ai/. Both correct.\n  • Themes: I drew it as its own cross-cutting concern but in tree it's a single file (src/constants/themes.ts) inside the core constants dir — smaller than the others. Plus a mirrored copy at src/transport/web/app/src/constants/theme.ts for the Docker build.\n  • src/weather/ (fetch.ts, wmo.ts) — a small standalone layer I didn't draw separately; it sits alongside core, called by tools/weather.ts.\n  • src/backups/ (backup cron) and src/settings.ts — infrastructure present in tree, not on my sketch.\n  • src/lib/, src/scripts/, src/tunnel.ts, src/combined.ts — utility/infra, not product layers.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },

